Body:
Reproduced on `zai-coding-plan/glm-5.2`, opencode **v1.17.8** (Linux). Ctrl+T shows no variants; effort stays at the default `high`.

Confirming the config-override workaround from the issue body works as expected — declaring variants under the provider makes both Ctrl+T cycling and `max` effort functional:

```jsonc
"provider": {
  "zai-coding-plan": {
    "models": {
      "glm-5.2": {
        "variants": {
          "high": { "reasoningEffort": "high" },
          "max":  { "reasoningEffort": "max" }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

…then `"agent": { "build": { "variant": "max" } }` to default to max. The `reasoningEffort` (camelCase) key in #32593 matches what works here in practice, so that special-case should resolve this cleanly once merged. 👍

### `packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts`
Modified the `runLoop` function to include:
```ts
          step++
          if (step === 1) {
            const cfg = yield* config.get()
            const skipTitleOption = cfg.provider?.[lastUser.model.providerID]?.models?.[lastUser.model.modelID]?.options?.["skip-title"]

            if (!(typeof skipTitleOption === "boolean" && skipTitleOption === true)) {
              yield* title({
                session,
                modelID: lastUser.model.modelID,
                providerID: lastUser.model.providerID,
                history: msgs,
              }).pipe(Effect.ignore, Effect.forkIn(scope))
            }
